10
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The Pursuit of Happyness is a 2006 American biographical drama film directed by Gabriele
Muccino and starring Will Smith as Chris Gardner, a homeless salesman.

11
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:27,000
Smith's son Jaden Smith co-stars, making his film
debut as Gardner's son, Christopher Jr.

12
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:18,000
The screenplay by Steven Conrad is based on the best-selling 2006 memoir
of the same name written by Gardner with Quincy Troupe.

13
01:16:03,000 --> 01:16:09,000
It is based on Gardner's nearly one-year struggle being homeless.

14
01:21:54,000 --> 01:22:00,000
The intentional misspelling of the film's title comes from a mural that Gardner
sees on the wall outside the daycare facility his son attended.

15
01:27:45,000 --> 01:27:51,000
The movie is set in San Francisco in 1981.

16
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
The film was released on December 15, 2006, by Columbia Pictures, and received positive reviews,
with Smith's performance and the emotional weight of the story garnering acclaim.

17
01:39:27,000 --> 01:39:33,000
Smith was nominated for an Academy Award and a Golden Globe for Best Actor.

18
01:45:18,000 --> 01:45:24,000
The film explores themes of work, worker, homeless person,
single parent, san francisco, california.

19
01:51:09,000 --> 01:51:15,000
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
